            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is similar to the use case discussed in #770.\r\n\r\nThis particular case of surrounding blockwise selection together with `$` will not be supported for at least the following reasons:\r\n- Actual implementation is not trivial while 'mini.surround' is already quite a big and complicated module.\r\n- It can be replicated with a macro. In this particular case: record macro with `qq`, `0sa$\"`, `k`, `q`; replay with `4Q`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This is similar to the use case discussed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2206372982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/770\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/770/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/770\">#770</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This particular case of surrounding blockwise selection together with <code class=\"notranslate\">$</code> will not be supported for at least the following reasons:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Actual implementation is not trivial while 'mini.surround' is already quite a big and complicated module.</li>\n<li>It can be replicated with a macro. In this particular case: record macro with <code class=\"notranslate\">qq</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">0sa$\"</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">k</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code>; replay with <code class=\"notranslate\">4Q</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "This is similar to the use case discussed in #770.\nThis particular case of surrounding blockwise selection together with $ will not be supported for at least the following reasons:\n\nActual implementation is not trivial while 'mini.surround' is already quite a big and complicated module.\nIt can be replicated with a macro. In this particular case: record macro with qq, 0sa$\", k, q; replay with 4Q.",
