                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "No, not really. All basic Vimscript tools (at least before Vim9script) are available in Neovim.\r\n\r\nIt is the fact that this specific example needs to be treated as special case with possibly not great workarounds (here is what looks like a relevant part of [vim-sandwich](https://github.com/machakann/vim-sandwich/blob/74cf93d58ccc567d8e2310a69860f1b93af19403/autoload/operator/sandwich.vim#L83-L107); I don't quite understand 'vim-surround' code) while being quite easily replaced with macro.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No, not really. All basic Vimscript tools (at least before Vim9script) are available in Neovim.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is the fact that this specific example needs to be treated as special case with possibly not great workarounds (here is what looks like a relevant part of <a href=\"https://github.com/machakann/vim-sandwich/blob/74cf93d58ccc567d8e2310a69860f1b93af19403/autoload/operator/sandwich.vim#L83-L107\">vim-sandwich</a>; I don't quite understand 'vim-surround' code) while being quite easily replaced with macro.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "No, not really. All basic Vimscript tools (at least before Vim9script) are available in Neovim.\nIt is the fact that this specific example needs to be treated as special case with possibly not great workarounds (here is what looks like a relevant part of vim-sandwich; I don't quite understand 'vim-surround' code) while being quite easily replaced with macro.",
